> The server runs in the background and streams its log; `stop SERVE`
> (or Esc in the ACTIONS menu) stops it. When the Ollama app already
> runs a server, Start is disabled.

> The access log lines ([GIN]) are left out: the panels ask every few
> seconds.

command SERVE
- run ollama serve 2>&1 | grep -v --line-buffered '\[GIN\]'
- output SERVER
- then refresh
- on_error refresh

command ASK
- run ./chat.py ask
- env MODEL=$MODEL PROMPT=$PROMPT WIDTH=$CHAT_WIDTH
- output CHAT
- then refresh

command NEW_CHAT
- run ./chat.py reset
- output CHAT

command UNLOAD
- run ollama stop "$MODEL"
- env MODEL=$MODEL
- output SERVER
- then refresh
